Date: Mon, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] bridge: drop SDL echo of ring-forwarded audio

The bridge PCM ring (0009) carries int16 mono/stereo controller audio to
JS. Feeding the SDL stream too doubles those sounds, so skip exactly the
ring-forwarded lanes in headless builds; anything else (e.g. float
altsound) still plays via SDL. Direct script PlaySound bypasses this
callback and is unaffected.

diff --git a/src/core/player.cpp b/src/core/player.cpp
--- a/src/core/player.cpp
+++ b/src/core/player.cpp
@@ -2845,6 +2892,16 @@ void Player::OnAudioUpdated(const unsigned int msgId, void *userData, void *msgD
    Player *me = static_cast<Player *>(userData);
    AudioUpdateMsg &msg = *static_cast<AudioUpdateMsg *>(msgData);
    std::lock_guard lock(me->m_audioSourceMutex);
+#ifdef VPX_HEADLESS_BRIDGE
+   // Only int16 mono/stereo controller audio is ring-forwarded (0009) and
+   // played from JS. Feeding the SDL stream too would double it, so drop
+   // it here; anything else (e.g. float altsound) still plays via SDL.
+   // Direct script PlaySound bypasses this callback and is unaffected.
+   if (msg.sampleFormat == CTLPI_AUDIO_FORMAT_SAMPLE_INT16 &&
+       (msg.channelFormat == CTLPI_AUDIO_FORMAT_CHANNEL_MONO ||
+        msg.channelFormat == CTLPI_AUDIO_FORMAT_CHANNEL_STEREO))
+      return;
+#endif
 
    auto laneIt = me->m_audioLanes.find(msg.sourceId.id);
    if (laneIt == me->m_audioLanes.end() || laneIt->second.overriden)
